# VoxelPort website: environment variables.
#
# The site needs NO secrets. It is a static build: everything the browser gets is public, and the pages only call
# public endpoints (the relays' /api/status and /api/servers, the uptime report, GitHub's public releases API).
# Do NOT put a secret in any variable that starts with VITE_: Vite copies those into the public JavaScript bundle.
#
# Nothing below has to be set for a normal deploy. Copy to .env.local only if you want to try a value locally
# (.env* files are git-ignored; this example file is the one exception and holds placeholders only).

# Set automatically by Vercel on every build: "production", "preview" or "development".
# scripts/prerender.mjs reads it: anything other than "production" builds noindex pages and a robots.txt that blocks
# crawlers, so preview URLs never get indexed. Unset (a local build) counts as production.
# Do not set this by hand in the Vercel dashboard. To test the preview behaviour locally:  VERCEL_ENV=preview npm run build
# VERCEL_ENV=

# Google AdSense. Both are public identifiers (they ship in the page source either way), so VITE_ is fine here.
# The loader script is already in index.html with the real publisher id (needed for AdSense's site review),
# so this only has to be set once you make an ad unit and want it to actually show. Leave unset and every
# <AdSlot> renders nothing — the site builds and works identically without them.
# VITE_ADSENSE_CLIENT=ca-pub-9089388412170867
# VITE_ADSENSE_SLOT_GUIDE=XXXXXXXXXX
